{# Used by all three /menu/ phases (browse, teach, drill) — restaurant
   name (centered) + a title/action row. The action itself (Train, "I'm
   Ready", or drill's "Back to Food") is passed in via {% call %} so the
   structure stays identical across every phase even though what's
   clickable differs by context — this is the one shared wrapper that
   replaced the old separate /learn/ page and its own divergent layout.

   showSwitcher renders the restaurant name as a dropdown (options =
   `restaurants`) instead of static text — Food/Drinks no longer toggle
   in-page (that's now the sidebar's Food/Drinks links, see nav.njk); the
   restaurant switcher moved here instead, in the same visual pattern
   (trigger + chevron + popover) that toggle used to use, per Erik's
   request. /menu/food/, /menu/drinks/, and /menu/food/{category} (etc.)
   are real, independently-visitable routes via Netlify rewrites
   (netlify.toml, status 200 — not a redirect, so the URL bar keeps
   showing the route the visitor actually requested) that silently serve
   this same file; the page script reads the real URL on load to pick the
   right content type (and category, if present) on a direct visit.
   showSwitcher is omitted on teach/drill — mid-flow isn't the place to
   jump to a different restaurant, so those phases get a plain static (or,
   for drill, JS-filled — see nameId/titleId) name.

   nameId/titleId: drill is one shared dynamic block (not baked per
   category, since chat transcripts are inherently dynamic), so its
   restaurant name + Food/Drinks title can't be server-rendered per
   category like teach's can — these let the page script target and
   fill them in once a drill starts. #}
{% macro venueHeader(restaurantName, title, showSwitcher=false, restaurants=[], nameId=false, titleId=false) %}
{% if showSwitcher %}
<div class="venue-switcher">
  <button class="menu-review__venue-name venue-switcher__trigger" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-label="Switch restaurant">
    <span class="venue-switcher__label">{{ restaurantName }}</span>
    <span class="venue-switcher__chevron" aria-hidden="true">▾</span>
  </button>
  <div class="venue-switcher__options" hidden>
    {% for restaurant in restaurants %}
    <button class="venue-switcher__option" type="button" data-restaurant-id="{{ restaurant.id }}">{{ restaurant.name }}</button>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
</div>
{% else %}
<p class="menu-review__venue-name"{% if nameId %} id="{{ nameId }}"{% endif %}>{{ restaurantName }}</p>
{% endif %}
<div class="page-header">
  <p class="page-title"{% if titleId %} id="{{ titleId }}"{% endif %}>{{ title }}</p>
  {{ caller() }}
</div>
{% endmacro %}
